course: dictionary
lesson: 2529
title: Decoys: tricks that lead you away
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A decoy is something used to trick someone, usually to lead them away from the real thing. Read the words around the word for clues: the sentence tells you what the decoy is for.
explain: «Some squid make an ink blob shaped like themselves as a decoy.» The blob is a fake copy that fools an attacker, so the squid can escape. Ask: would "a trick" fit here? If yes, you have the right meaning.
explain: Decoy can also be a verb. To decoy someone is to trick them into going somewhere else, like a hunter using a wooden duck to draw real ducks closer. Look for the clues: fake, trick, lead away.
fact: A decoy is a person or thing used to trick someone and lead them away or into a trap.
fact: A decoy can be a model of a bird, such as a wooden duck, that hunters use to attract real birds.
fact: To decoy someone means to trick them in this way.
fact: «Some squid make an ink blob shaped like themselves as a decoy.»
fact: In sport, a decoy runner draws defenders away so that a teammate can get free.
exercise: «Some squid make an ink blob shaped like themselves as a decoy.» What is the decoy for? | To make the squid look bigger for its friends | To keep the squid warm in cold water | *To trick an attacker and help the squid escape | To show the squid is hungry
exercise: A hunter sets a wooden duck on the pond to attract real ducks. What is the wooden duck? | A pond rescue boat | A real duck with a hurt wing | *A decoy | A new kind of fishing net
exercise: In a game, a decoy runner draws defenders away. What does the decoy runner do? | Keeps the score | *Draws defenders away from the player with the ball | Sits on the bench and rests | Carries the ball into the goal
test: «A bird pretends to have a broken wing to lead a fox away from its nest.» What is the bird doing? | *Acting as a decoy to trick the fox | Trying to fly south for the winter | Asking the fox for help | Hiding its eggs under a leaf
test: Which word means to trick someone into going somewhere else? | To deliver | *To decoy | To declare | To decorate
exam: The squid's ink blob is a decoy. What does a decoy do? | It shows how old the squid is | It cleans the water around the squid | *It tricks an attacker into looking the wrong way | It makes a loud noise to warn others
